  "sessionFileNote": "The session file's disappearance is a race with the close, and neither field settles it. In the first pass sessionFileGone was false for all 18 sessions — the <session>.pid file was still on disk in the instant the close returned — and by the time the record was read back the campaign's own session files were gone, leaving only the three foreign ones. In the second pass the same field was false and the first re-check, microseconds later, found the file gone (sessionFileGoneAfterMs 0). So the file is removed while the client is still returning, and both readings are artifacts of when the check happened. From the second pass on each close samples the file every 200 ms for up to 20000 ms and records the first re-check at which it was missing in sessionFileGoneAfterMs — -1 means it was already gone when the close returned, 0 that the first re-check missed it, null that it was still there when the sampling gave up. Sessions from the first pass carry no sample."
